<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - March 21.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - March 21.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 03/21/97  03/14/97  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	     13.84     21.40     5.95	 9.20	6.3</p>
<p>West	     43.52     50.10    16.80	19.33     27.1</p>
<p>Total Canada   57.36     71.50    11.67	14.54     17.3</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 03/21/97: 232.55 bcf, 03/14/97: 232.55 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 03/21/97: 259.11 bcf, 03/14/96: 259.11 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S.</p>
<p>((--Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
